# Retail data (port/docs/retail-eu-plan.md): r20b, the way down into the hedge maze. The European
# discs' r20b closes the stairs from the ledge for Easy: trigger area 0x1C is a collision wall across
# their top and room model group 0xA6 the railing over it (the debug build's discs have neither). The
# European R20bInit (st2_1.rel, text 0x10F44, read with retail_code.py and the module's relocations)
# opens them for the difficulties above Easy (a byte their game sets to game_mode > 3, cleared in the
# bonus games): SceAtSetEnable(0x1C, 0), SmdSetTrans(0xA6, 0). On Easy the maze stays shut and the room
# behaves as after the moonstone door: room flag 1, model groups 0x86..0x8A and item areas 0x80..0x82,
# 0x88 off, the boxes 9, 10, 14, 15 destroyed, no radio call, entry camera or enemies. This build has
# neither branch, so with the European discs nobody got down there (tester report and owner's test on
# the Retroid, 28.10.2026). Both branches as their code, the byte read from game_mode. Nothing changes
# with the debug build's discs. A port patch for retail data.
# Also the Japanese discs (port/docs/retail-jp-plan.md, J4: their code is the European one here).
--- a/src/st2/r20b.cpp
+++ b/src/st2/r20b.cpp
@@ -85,6 +85,15 @@
 void Evt_R20BS00_Func(Event* e, u32);
 void EvtTexRenderCamTrans(Event* e, int cut);
 
+extern "C" int re4_disc_retail_eu(void), re4_disc_retail_jp(void); /* port: runtime/dvd.cpp */
+
+/* port: the European releases' "maze open" byte (pG + 0x4F9F there): above Easy, not in the bonus games
+   (patch 0138) */
+static int R20bMazeOpen()
+{
+    return pG->game_mode > 3 && !SysFlagChk(pG, SYS_OMAKE_ADA_GAME) && !SysFlagChk(pG, SYS_OMAKE_ETC_GAME);
+}
+
 // Room init for the great hall. Until the s00 event has played, the room is pre-loaded with its
 // enemy and area 2 runs the event. The locked door waits for its key.
 void R20bInit()
@@ -96,6 +105,38 @@
 
 #line 60 "D:/Bio4/Prog/r20b.cpp"
     r20b_work = (R20bWork*) MEM_CALLOC(sizeof(R20bWork), 1, 0xd);
+    /* port: the hedge maze by difficulty with retail data, as the European R20bInit (patch 0138) */
